# sprint12_typestate_fs_verify_part2.oot — (Part 2 of sprint12_typestate_fs_verify.oot)
# Continuation of `openOODA/audit/sprint12_typestate_fs_verify.oot`.

## 4. Process args
`process_args(p)` → `oo_sys_args(p)` (`process.oo:15-17`).
SHIPPED `:31` matches.

C (`chs_rt_sys.c:442-467`):
  `oo_cap_require_process` (ProcessCap or legacy SysCap, `:190-196`)
  read `/proc/self/cmdline` into 4096-byte buf
  `fread(..., sizeof(buf)-1)` — 4095 bytes
  skip first NUL field (argv0)
  push later fields
  no `buf[n]='\0'`; trailing fragment without NUL is dropped

Long argv truncates. argv0 is omitted. Last partial arg is lost.
Residual, named. Product behavior, not a cap hole.

## 5. Typestate on check
`main.oo:26-32` imports tok/parse/walk/join/match/fn + `check_typestate.oo`.
Not `check_typestate_call.oo`. Prior audit line 69 is false.

`check_drive.oo:79-105` order:
  secret sinks
  type checks (ann, undef, arity, immut, mut, unary, cmp, if/while,
  logic, missing return, refinements)
  then `check_typestate(src, toks)` at line 105
  then more type checks (must-use, call lits, field, struct)

Prior audit said `:98`. Live is `:105`.

`check_typestate.oo:16-21`: parse directives from `src`; if no
`__tsf__` fn, return; else `ts_walk_program`.

Parse (`check_typestate_parse.oo`):
  `// TYPESTATE: Type S1 S2` → machine, states stored as `Type#S`
  `// TYPESTATE fn name: From -> To` and `-> To`
  `// TYPESTATE end S` → `__tsend__Type`
  unknown From/To refused
  two machines must not share a raw state name? Board
  `TYPE_STATE.oot:36` says state names are global and two machines
  must not share a name. Parse keys `__tss__` as `Type#state` so
  `Sock Open` and `File Open` can both exist (`:146`). Board line
  22 agrees. Line 36 conflicts with line 22. Residual docs, not
  a code hole. `typestate_two_types.oo` is a smoke OK case.

Walk:
  paren call and `s.fn()` (`check_typestate_walk.oo:113-134`)
  first arg must be a bare IDENT (`:52-64`); nested call / field
  / index yields empty arg and is refused on From→To
  let/assign alias (`:92-95`, `:143-146`)
  ctor `>To` (`:101-102`)

Fn compose (`check_typestate_fn.oo:134-174`):
  body text that calls another TYPESTATE fn sets `__tscompose__`
  live exit must leave first param as To
  leaf body trusts the directive
  process_exit does not require To (`check_typestate_join.oo:229-235`)
  param rebind refused (`:126-132`)

Join (`check_typestate_join.oo`):
  if/else both sides same state; missing else keeps pre
  return / process_exit mark `__tsdiv__` and do not join
  while/for body must leave pre states unchanged
  transition in if/loop condition refused (`:168-170`, `:215-217`)
  match arms join like if/else (`check_typestate_match.oo:12-45`)

`ts_merge_branch` builds a fresh env of `__tsv__` names from the
pre bag (`:51-95`). `__tsa__` alias links are not copied. Use of
an alias after if/else can fail closed (“no state”). Residual.
Not a bypass.

Cache: `check_cache_tree_key` prefix `t_ts3_` (`check_cache.oo:69-72`).
Old OK without typestate is not reused. Prior audit said `:63`. Live `:70`.

Rails exist: `scripts/typestate_check_smoke.oo`, fixtures listed in
`TYPE_STATE.oot:53-70` plus more in the script (`:26-69`).
This audit did not execute them.

## 6. np>12 — FAIL vs prior PASS
Prior audit: “`check_mod.oo` prepends `ts_extract_dir_src`”.
Live `check_mod.oo:53-86` when `np > 12`:

  collect paths
  scan fn names into depth-0 binds
  `body = strip_import_lines(raw2)`
  `run_check_core_binds(sys, body, binds)`
  print OK

`strip_import_lines` (`check_collect.oo:141-172`) drops import
lines only. Same-file `// TYPESTATE` comments stay.

There is no extract. There is no prepend. Grep of ooda/ for
`ts_extract` is empty.

Small graphs `np <= 12` use `load_source_with_imports`.
`load_import.oo:76-79` keeps non-import chunks, including comments.
`typestate_cross_ok.oo` imports `typestate_lib.oo` (directives in
the lib). That works only on the concat path.

Large graphs: a consumer file without its own TYPESTATE lines
parses no `__tsf__` and `check_typestate` returns at
`check_typestate.oo:18-20`. Transitions in that file are not
checked. `TYPE_STATE.oot:25` already says “small graphs”.
`:41` “No inter-file lattice.”
SHIPPED `:49` “Imports keep directives.” is wider than the code.

## 7. Heap alias / field store
`TYPE_STATE.oot:21` let-alias share one lifecycle via `__tsa__`
(`check_typestate_fn.oo:112-119`). Depth cap 16 (`:93`).
No heap object identity. No struct-field store lattice.
`// TYPESTATE` does not watch `Box` or field writes.
Named residual. Board agrees.

